          "score": 0.6532984375953674,
          "snippet": "The Ixos Protocol faces a critical operational paradox: it aims to deliver instantaneous, semantic file retrieval on hardware constraints that typically preclude such capabilities. The current baseline latency of 17 seconds for a 30,000-file dataset\u2014comprising 3 seconds of model initialization and 14 seconds of search execution\u2014renders the system functionally unusable for the high-velocity workflows of the target demographic: privacy-conscious knowledge workers. To bridge the gap between this 17-second reality and the sub-2-second perceptual requirement, a fundamental re-architecture of the \"Hybrid Cascade\" system is required. This report proposes a shift from a synchronous, monolithic processing model to an asynchronous, speculative, and highly pipelined architecture driven by advanced systems programming concepts available in the Rust ecosystem.  "
